{
"segments": [
{
"text": "Case Eight.",
"start": 0.75,
"end": 1.71,
"pause": 0.6
},
{
"text": "The Four Bakers.",
"start": 2.31,
"end": 3.526,
"pause": 1.4
},
{
"text": "Jago Penhallow's cinnamon buns are famous along the whole coast. Every Saturday he bakes a tray of twelve and sets it on the cooling rack by the back door of the bakery.",
"start": 4.926,
"end": 15.593,
"pause": 0.85
},
{
"text": "This Saturday, while Jago was serving at the front, the whole tray disappeared.",
"start": 16.442999999999998,
"end": 20.965,
"pause": 0.85
},
{
"text": "Four people had passed the back door in the right ten minutes: Pip Carew, Demelza Rowe, Mr Fenwick the grocer, and Kerensa Hale. Jago, who was in a terrible mood about his buns, marched all four into the Kettle and Gull and asked Agnes Bell to sort it out.",
"start": 21.815,
"end": 38.071,
"pause": 0.85
},
{
"text": "Agnes listened to each of them in turn.",
"start": 38.921,
"end": 41.396,
"pause": 0.85
},
{
"text": "Pip said, \"Demelza took them.\"",
"start": 42.246,
"end": 44.123,
"pause": 0.85
},
{
"text": "Demelza said, \"Kerensa took them.\"",
"start": 44.973,
"end": 47.171,
"pause": 0.85
},
{
"text": "Mr Fenwick said, \"I didn't take them.\"",
"start": 48.021,
"end": 50.282,
"pause": 0.85
},
{
"text": "Kerensa said, \"Demelza is lying.\"",
"start": 51.132,
"end": 53.521,
"pause": 0.85
},
{
"text": "Then Jago, still cross, added one more thing. \"I know this lot. And I know for a fact that just one of them is telling the truth today. The other three are all fibbing.\"",
"start": 54.371,
"end": 64.931,
"pause": 0.85
},
{
"text": "Agnes raised an eyebrow, but she knew Jago was right about one thing: he did know this lot.",
"start": 65.781,
"end": 71.179,
"pause": 0.85
},
{
"text": "Here are the statements again. Pip: Demelza took them. Demelza: Kerensa took them. Mr Fenwick: I didn't take them. Kerensa: Demelza is lying. Exactly one of the four is telling the truth. One person took the buns.",
"start": 72.029,
"end": 87.069,
"pause": 1.1
},
{
"text": "Can you solve it? Who took the cinnamon buns?",
"start": 88.169,
"end": 90.707,
"pause": 1.2
},
{
"text": "Think about it.",
"start": 91.907,
"end": 92.931,
"pause": 0.9
},
{
"text": "Take a moment, or pause here if you are listening. When you are ready, the solution follows.",
"start": 93.831,
"end": 99.058,
"pause": 4.5
},
{
"text": "The Solution.",
"start": 103.558,
"end": 104.582,
"pause": 1.1
},
{
"text": "Mr Fenwick took the buns.",
"start": 105.682,
"end": 107.303,
"pause": 0.85
},
{
"text": "Look at Demelza and Kerensa. Kerensa says that Demelza is lying. If Demelza is telling the truth, then Kerensa is wrong. If Demelza is lying, then Kerensa is right. Either way, exactly one of those two is telling the truth.",
"start": 108.153,
"end": 123.727,
"pause": 0.85
},
{
"text": "Since only one person in the whole group is telling the truth, and that person is either Demelza or Kerensa, both Pip and Mr Fenwick must be fibbing.",
"start": 124.577,
"end": 134.305,
"pause": 0.85
},
{
"text": "Mr Fenwick said, I didn't take them. If that is a fib, then he did take them. And Pip's statement, that Demelza took them, is false, which also fits. Kerensa turns out to be the single truthful one.",
"start": 135.155,
"end": 148.253,
"pause": 0.85
},
{
"text": "Mr Fenwick confessed. He said that he had been trying for years to work out Jago's secret recipe and had only meant to take one bun to study, but they smelled so good that he panicked and took the lot. Jago, secretly flattered, let him off on the condition that Mr Fenwick never tried to copy them again.",
"start": 149.103,
"end": 168.218,
"pause": 0.0
}
],
